<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.14.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00319</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.14.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a17a8484-7cc7-48f1-b301-b6c45ac0f4b9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para id="para-00002"><quote id="quote-00001">In questions 1 - 5, choose an equation of a line parallel to the given line and contains the given point. The choices are in slope-intercept form.</quote></para>
      <exercise id="_909f5114-1beb-4172-83b5-3cfc322d081c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Line \(y = 4x + 2\) Point \((1, 2)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00004">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00005">\(y=4x+2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00006">\(y=4x-2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00007">\(y=-\frac14x-2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00008">\(y=-\frac14x+2\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00009">Correct! \(y=4x-2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00010">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00011">The correct answer is \(y = 4 x -2\).</para>
          <para id="para-00012">The slope of a line parallel to \(y = 4x + 2\) is 4. The line contains the point (1,2).</para>
          <para id="para-00013">\(\begin{aligned}y − y_1 &amp;= m(x − x_1)\\ y − (2) &amp;= 4(x − (1))\\ y − 2 &amp;= 4(x − 1)\\ y − 2 &amp;= 4x − 4\\ y &amp;= 4x − 2 \end{aligned}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_61d898ac-c69c-4b32-8003-4768a55fa342" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00014">Line \(y = -3x -1\) Point \((2, -3)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00015">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00016">\(y=-3x +3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00017">\(y=-3x-3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00018">\(y=\frac13x+3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00019">\(y=\frac13x-3\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00020">Correct! \(y=-3x +3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00022">The correct answer is \(y = -3x +3\).</para>
          <para id="para-00023">The slope of a line parallel to \(y = −3x − 1\) is \(−3\). The line contains the point (2,−3).</para>
          <para id="para-00024">\(\begin{aligned}y − y_1 &amp;= m(x − x_1)\\ y − (-3) &amp;= −3(x − (2))\\ y + 3 &amp;= −3(x − 2)\\ y +3 &amp;= −3x + 6\\ y &amp;= −3x +3 \end{aligned}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_39322255-26c6-4b83-98b0-7e16753f6a4c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00025">Line \(2x - y = 6\) Point \((3, 0)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00026">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00027">\(y=2x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00028">\(y=-2x+6\)</para>
          <para id="para-00029">\(y=-2x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00030">\(y=2x-6\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00031">Correct! \(y=2x-6\)</para>
          <para id="para-00032">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00033">The correct answer is \(y=2x-6\).</para>
          <para id="para-00034">The slope of a line parallel to \(2x −y = 6\) is 2. The line contains the point (3,0).</para>
          <para id="para-00035">\(\begin{aligned}y − y_1 &amp;= m(x − x_1)\\ y − (0) &amp;= 2(x − (3))\\ y &amp;= 2(x − 3)\\ y &amp;= 2x − 6\\ \end{aligned}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_72376f8b-6771-4aa4-8484-40c9d04b1f19" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00036">Line \(x = -4\) Point \((-3, -5)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00037">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00038">\(x=-3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00039">\(y=-5\)</para>
          <para id="para-00040">\(x=-5\)</para>
          <para id="para-00041">\(y=-4\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00042">Correct! \(x=-3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00043">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00044">The correct answer is \(x=-3\).</para>
          <para id="para-00045">The slope of a line parallel to \(x = −4\) is undefined. The line contains the point (−3,−5). The only equation with an undefined slope passing through (−3,−5) is \(x = −3\). The only equation with an undefined slope passing through (−3,−5) is \(x = −3\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="e11b16ef-f53c-40c9-bf63-f5f54930aa72" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00046">Line \(y = 5\) Point \((2, -2)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00047">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00048">\(x=2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00049">\(x=5\)</para>
          <para id="para-00050">\(y=-2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00051">\(y=2\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00052">Correct! \(y=-2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00053">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00054">The correct answer is \(y=-2\).</para>
          <para id="para-00055">The slope of a line parallel to \(y = 5\) is 0. The line contains the point (2,−2). The only equation with a slope of 0 passing through (2, −2) is \(y = −2\). The only equation with a slope of 0 passing through (2, −2) is \(y = −2\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5980b1f7-cf0a-4fbc-94a4-7a42d531e127" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00056"><quote id="quote-00002">In questions 6 – 10, find an equation of a line that is perpendicular to the given line and contains the given point. The choices are in slope-intercept form.</quote></para>
          <para id="para-00057">Line \(y = -2x +3\) Point \((2, 2)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00058">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00059">\(y=-2x+6\)</para>
          <para id="para-00060">\(y=-\frac12x+3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00061">\(y=\frac12x+3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00062">\(y=\frac12x+1\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00063">Correct! \(y=\frac12x+1\)</para>
          <para id="para-00064">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00065">The correct answer is \(y=\frac12x+1\).</para>
          <para id="para-00066">TThe slope of a line perpendicular to \(y = −2x + 3\) is \(\frac12\). The line contains the point (2,2).</para>
          <para id="para-00067">\(\begin{aligned}y − y_1 &amp;= m(x − x_1)\\ y − (2) &amp;= \frac12(x − (2))\\ y −2 &amp;= \frac12(x − 2)\\ y −2 &amp;= \frac12x − 1\\ y &amp;= \frac12x + 1 \end{aligned}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_34f5f688-d8a6-44c9-ad20-c0035d7de4f2" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00068">Line \(y = -x +5\) Point \((3, 3)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00069">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00070">\(y=-x+6\)</para>
          <para id="para-00071">\(y=x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00072">\(y=x+5\)</para>
          <para id="para-00073">\(y=-x+3\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00074">Correct! \(y=x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00075">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00076">The correct answer is \(y=x\).</para>
          <para id="para-00077">The slope of a line perpendicular to \(y = −x + 5\) is 1. The line contains the point (3,3).</para>
          <para id="para-00078">\(\begin{aligned}y − y_1 &amp;= m(x − x_1)\\ y − (3) &amp;= 1(x − (3))\\ y − 3 &amp;= 1(x − 3)\\ y − 3 &amp;= x − 3\\ y &amp;= x \\ \end{aligned}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3854c9ff-58ec-4025-9fbb-4ee11fad4cae" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00079">Line \(y = \frac{3}{4}x - 2\) Point \((-3, 4)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00080">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00081">\(y=-\frac43x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00082">\(y=-\frac43x+4\)</para>
          <para id="para-00083">\(y=\frac34x+4\)</para>
          <para id="para-00084">\(y=\frac34x+\frac{17}4\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00085">Correct! \(y=-\frac43x\)</para>
          <para id="para-00086">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00087">The correct answer is \(y=-\frac43x\).</para>
          <para id="para-00088">The slope of a line perpendicular to \(y = \frac34x − 2\) is \(−\frac43.\) The line contains the point (−3,4).</para>
          <para id="para-00089">\(\begin{aligned}y − y_1 &amp;= m(x − x_1)\\ y − (4) &amp;= −\frac43(x − (−3))\\ y −4 &amp;= −\frac43(x + 3)\\ y −4 &amp;= −\frac43x − 4\\ y &amp;= −\frac43x \end{aligned}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_69dbb715-5c57-4a0a-b43b-7937bcb9423c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00090">Line \(x = -5\) Point \((1, -2)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00091">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00092">\(y=-5\)</para>
          <para id="para-00093">\(x=1\)</para>
          <para id="para-00094">\(y=-2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00095">\(x=-2\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00096">Correct! \(y=-2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00097">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00098">The correct answer is \(y=-2\).</para>
          <para id="para-00099">The slope of a line perpendicular to \(x = −5\) is 0. The line contains the point (1,−2). The only equation with a slope of 0 passing through (1,−2) is y \(= −2\). The only equation with a slope of 0 passing through (1,−2) is y \(= −2\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_61146fd3-06de-4520-a2b4-fc2d65f3e87d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00100">Line \(y - 3 = 0\) Point \((-2, -4)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00101">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00102">\(y=33\)</para>
          <para id="para-00103">\(y=-4\)</para>
          <para id="para-00104">\(x=3\)</para>
          <para id="para-00105">\(x=-2\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00106">Correct! \(x=-2\)</para>
          <para id="para-00107">Try again. Revisit activity 1.14.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00108">The correct answer is \(x=-2\).</para>
          <para id="para-00109">The slope of a line parallel to \(y −3 = 0\) is undefined. The line contains the point (−2,−4). The only equation with an undefined slope passing through (−2,−4) is \(x = −2\). The only equation with an undefined slope passing through (−2,−4) is \(x = −2\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
